  "implementation": [
    "The existing BTX reader and compatibility preparation/plan/bind/run APIs retain compressed atom rows for native SM103 execution",
    "P22/P33/P24/P43/P44 support ordinary and coupled MCG/SQG E4M3 records across complete 256-channel pairs",
    "Preparation reverses BTX rate-byte nibbles, restores record-major scale order and retains global coupled draw/input-scale-half coordinates",
    "The static paired layout selects low/high 128-channel records; runtime metadata guards reject rates outside the declared BTX pair vocabulary",
    "Int64 offsets, prewarmed capacity callables, stable storage and graph replay share the canonical atom backend",
    "SM12x retains its existing coalesced single-pair implementation and narrower supported rate/transform sets"
  ],
